{"author":{"id":"53b38b4189542570b1a723cdea9ea54af99104fbc59b44537f04a0e63f4629c5"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795290101,"nonce":"TAHYM4ZV+1pLgv1cU7LX19Wffy0=","title":"L7 — Serve the site at morghulis.buildwitharkye.me","message":"## Context\nVercel project `morghulis` (personal scope, `vcp` = `vercel -Q ~/.vercel-personal`, repo ARKye03/morghulis-website) only has `morghulis.vercel.app`. buildwitharkye.me is registered and DNS-hosted at Namecheap (`dns1/dns2.registrar-servers.com`); apex + www point to project `starting-for-here` and must keep working. Namecheap MCP lives in the `portfolio-agent` session.\n\n## Approach\n- `vcp domains add morghulis.buildwitharkye.me morghulis`; read the CNAME target Vercel reports\n- Namecheap: add CNAME host `morghulis` → that target. `namecheap.domains.dns.setHosts` replaces the whole record set: read current hosts first and resend every existing record plus the new one\n- Set project Node.js version to 24.x (matches L1 `.nvmrc`/`engines`)\n- Trigger production deploy of trunk if needed; `vcp domains inspect` until verified\n\n## Depends on\nL1 — Node 24 engines (project setting must match)\n\n## Out of scope\n- Apex or www of buildwitharkye.me\n- Code changes\n\n## Open\n- Needs Namecheap access: run via portfolio-agent or by hand; an impl subagent may lack the MCP\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- `dig +short morghulis.buildwitharkye.me` resolves to Vercel\n- https://morghulis.buildwitharkye.me returns 200 with valid TLS and serves the trunk build\n- https://buildwitharkye.me and https://www.buildwitharkye.me still serve starting-for-here\n- Project `morghulis` Node version 24.x","files":null}]}